1815 0 obj
<<
  /Type /StructElem
  /S /Figure
  /P 1814 0 R
  /Alt (Screenshot of the Copernicus Land Monitoring Service (CLMS) CLC+ Query Builder interface, specifically the 'Text' tab, used for defining rules for 'Output Class '2 - FL Deciduous''. The interface displays a rule editor with a main rule expression area, a 'Rule Structure' section providing syntax guidance, and an 'Examples' section. The main rule, commented as '# Intersect HRL with CLC+ BB classes', is composed of two conditional blocks joined by the logical operator '&&' (AND). These conditions use `sumCov` functions to check the percentage coverage of specified EAGLE elements and their associated barcodes: 1. The first conditional block is: `(sumCov('LCC-trees', 5) >= 30 && sumCov('LCH-broad-leaved', 2) >= 30)`. This requires the summed coverage of 'LCC-trees' with barcode '5' to be at least 30% AND the summed coverage of 'LCH-broad-leaved' with barcode '2' to be at least 30%. 2. The second conditional block is: `(sumCov('LCC-trees', 5) >= 30 && sumCov('LCH-deciduous', 5) >= 30 && sumCov('LCH-broad-leaved', 5) >= 30)`. This requires the summed coverage of 'LCC-trees' (barcode 5), 'LCH-deciduous' (barcode 5), and 'LCH-broad-leaved' (barcode 5) to each be at least 30%. The 'Rule Structure' section provides generic syntax for `firstCov` expressions: - `firstCov('<EAGLE_ELEMENT_IDENTIFIER>', <BARCODE>) <OPERATOR> firstCov('<EAGLE_ELEMENT_IDENTIFIER>', <BARCODE>)...` - `firstCov('<EAGLE_ELEMENT_IDENTIFIER>', <BARCODE> [// <BARCODE>/*]) <OPERATOR> <VALUE>...` The 'Examples' section clarifies rule formulation: - 'When comparing coverage against coverage, only one barcode is allowed in each coverage expression,' as shown in `firstCov('LCC-water', 3) >= firstCov('LCC-trees', 5)`. - 'When comparing coverage against value, multiple barcodes are allowed,' as shown in `firstCov('LCC-water', 3 // 4 // 5) >= 30`. Partially visible text indicates that this comparison with multiple barcodes is equivalent to an OR-connected ruleset. The interface also includes buttons for 'Computation manual' and 'EAGLE-Elements', along with 'CANCEL' and 'ADD' action buttons.)
  /A [<<
    /O /Layout
    /Placement /Block
  >>]
  /K [0]
  /Pg 4793 0 R
>>
endobj

